#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186187994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188290 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9609247-0e03-57ea-b5ae-e4d8317f21cd" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Contextual Problems Into Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "67d01a20-4e4b-5b03-a2a3-f4b21cd81662" :question/math-academy-id "e-10072" :question/problem "Since the year $2000$, a herd of antelopes multiplies at a rate proportional to their population. Also, the number of antelopes in the herd decreases by $20$ antelopes per year due to predators. What differential equation describes the rate of change in the population of antelopes at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in years) since the year $2000?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change in the number of antelopes per year increases in proportion to $P$ and decreases by $20.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}P}{\\textrm{d}t}=kP - 20,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a (positive) constant of proportionality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186187995 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba211dba-23ad-5755-b1e3-082e13be59a2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Three-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "1b0483b6-a42d-51fb-9ccd-fe6cb2a7acc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-10075" :question/problem "The volume of a sphere increases at a rate inversely proportional to its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process." :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a sphere **increases** at a rate **inversely proportional** to its **radius**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a sphere* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}$ *increases* at a rate *inversely proportional to its radius.* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = \\dfrac{k}{r},\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a sphere is given by\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =4\\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ 4\\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{(\\frac{k}{r})}{4\\pi {r}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{4\\pi {r}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK = \\dfrac{k}{4\\pi} > 0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{K}{r^3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186187996 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "474f9c82-4ae7-58e0-9457-6bda9cab8973" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Coordinate Plane Problems Into Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b657adbb-c3c4-54c2-8c2c-44ccc0bf9c3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10076" :question/problem "At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the derivative $y'(x)$ is **inversely** proportional to the square of the distance from $P$ to the origin. The derivative at the point $(-1,2)$ equals $2.$ What differential equation describes this curve?" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the **derivative** $y'(x)$ is **inversely proportional** to the **square of the distance from $P$ to the origin.** *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The *square of the distance from $P$ to the origin* is given by $x^2+y^2.$\n\n- Since the *derivative* is *inversely proportional to* the square of the distance from $P$ to the origin, we have \n\n$$\ny'(x) = k\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x^2+y^2}\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant.\n\nSo, our differential equation is\n\n$$\ny'(x) = \\dfrac{k}{x^2+y^2}.\n$$\n\nIn addition, we're told that $y'(x) = 2$ when at the point $(-1, 2).$ We can use this to determine the value of the coefficient $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{k}{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{k}{5} \\\\ k & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the differential equation describing the curve is\n\n$$\ny'(x)= \\dfrac{10}{x^2+y^2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188203 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d868c89-ca9e-589d-917e-cfec472a44f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Two-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "012abf23-a2df-5479-a38f-3c76c099a39f" :question/math-academy-id "e-524" :question/problem "The area of a circle decreases at a rate that's proportional to its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process." :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **area** of a circle **decreases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to its **radius**. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *area $A$ of a circle* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t}$ *decreases* at a rate that's *proportional* to its *radius.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t} = -kr\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}.$\n\nThe area of a circle is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\pi r^2.\n$$\n\n \n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-kr \\\\ 2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-kr \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{kr}{2\\pi r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK = \\dfrac{k}{2\\pi} > 0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t} = -K.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d868c89-ca9e-589d-917e-cfec472a44f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Two-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80d7ad93-ced2-5cb6-b8e6-831b077f527f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = r + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185533} {:answer/id #uuid "8283f08a-44c9-5156-914a-adeb407f14d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = Kr^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185534} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ecce28-f1c0-5ad5-8938-93bca607e9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = Kr" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185535} {:answer/id #uuid "f27f4060-33cd-58cb-9623-2b9d57ca80ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185536} {:answer/id #uuid "48e52784-b8f9-5bf0-af0e-aa8c89badafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = Kt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185537}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e2c35a2-00a1-5395-9ca6-d665e10ade6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185532}] :question/id #uuid "c8d1bea5-b961-5d22-9bfd-ba62f26db131" :question/math-academy-id "q-119161" :question/problem "The area of a circle increases at a rate that's proportional to the square of its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t)$, in this process. Assume that $K > 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188290 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9609247-0e03-57ea-b5ae-e4d8317f21cd" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Contextual Problems Into Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7871ed-5cf7-50d7-886e-dbe5d153b9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB-250,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373717} {:answer/id #uuid "e7dfbae4-5b1d-5477-8e3d-b60d9435539f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250t,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373718} {:answer/id #uuid "44700f85-a5f3-5ba3-b3be-7e5afb18cd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB+250,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373719} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6edff6-d4af-5c48-a54d-c54c74640bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k{B}^{2}-250,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373720} {:answer/id #uuid "724c6b53-f1f0-58e4-8ecf-980b9958ff52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "724c6b53-f1f0-58e4-8ecf-980b9958ff52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373721} :answer-field/id #uuid "497d4119-43d8-54a4-9409-872704d2bb05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30342124-81c8-53c0-b466-7bdc97912fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-119189" :question/problem "A scientist experiments with bacteria. The number of bacteria $B(t)$ in his experiment increases at a rate proportional to the number of bacteria at that moment. Additionally, due to environmental conditions, $250$ bacteria die every hour.\nWhat is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the population of bacteria at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time in hours?" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change in the number of bacteria per hour increases in proportion to $B$ and decreases by $250.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=kB-250,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a (positive) constant of proportionality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373799 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba211dba-23ad-5755-b1e3-082e13be59a2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Three-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a327b9-75a5-53f6-8b43-cf618bcf3524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=K{s}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373801} {:answer/id #uuid "1df99bf7-929a-5903-abcf-591bb526f29e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373802} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbf909f-462f-5518-8013-a606f7cf41aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373803} {:answer/id #uuid "3d49d7ac-08ee-59ab-9b44-461517ebb9fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{s}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373804} {:answer/id #uuid "708d1932-73c6-5f7d-ae3b-5e1d6d9045b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=K{s}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bbf909f-462f-5518-8013-a606f7cf41aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{s}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373803} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ed6ed5-0a52-5e29-8c5e-f028a3e0baf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "deb34ff2-c563-5932-95e2-cff733776593" :question/math-academy-id "q-143125" :question/problem "The volume of a cube increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the length of its edge. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the edge length, $s(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a cube **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **length of its edge**.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a cube* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ *increases* at a rate that's *inversely proportional to the length of its edge.* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cube is given by\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({s}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{s} \\\\ 3{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{s} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{3{s}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{3}>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{s}^{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d868c89-ca9e-589d-917e-cfec472a44f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Two-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44aa8350-415a-5f9c-b0de-81bc08e238c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-Kr" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373822} {:answer/id #uuid "f1641817-2c87-59b4-b4f0-67eb29c03041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373823} {:answer/id #uuid "f685a9e1-aaf6-5e7b-a9e6-a1f060c8d1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373824} {:answer/id #uuid "b877dcdf-d8f4-5a0a-ad47-fe6c14197fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373825} {:answer/id #uuid "d94f34bd-600c-5304-a9c0-6d081c68ab35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=K{r}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1641817-2c87-59b4-b4f0-67eb29c03041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373823} :answer-field/id #uuid "96d00b91-6897-5427-9c98-70d18a8a25c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdeb725d-e8ab-53b6-a397-2087096b75de" :question/math-academy-id "q-143131" :question/problem "The area of a circle decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **area** of a circle **decreases** at a **rate** that's **inversely proportional** to its **radius**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *area $A$ of a circle* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate that's *inversely proportional* to its *radius.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{r}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe area of a circle is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ 2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k}{2\\pi {r}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{2\\pi }>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{K}{{r}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d868c89-ca9e-589d-917e-cfec472a44f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Two-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0fb4ff0-8aba-56c6-bf18-44b6befa2526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373843} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0b3c0e-b662-5862-a4c5-679402ce0bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=K{A}^{5/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373844} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3d4487-e746-5e3c-9c6e-dc0aa305a8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373845} {:answer/id #uuid "c4368a2d-1df2-525b-96d3-28c62a09439d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373846} {:answer/id #uuid "c54d10a3-7468-590f-b69a-d71e43ed2923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=KA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd3d4487-e746-5e3c-9c6e-dc0aa305a8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373845} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7d7a9b-3a3b-5028-ad76-6fd5d5b5cf8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20695e23-caba-5b56-9712-3007924a9859" :question/math-academy-id "q-143136" :question/problem "The side length of a square decreases at a rate proportional to its area. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the area, $A(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **side length** of a square **decreases** at a rate **proportional** to its **area**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *side length $s$ of a square* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate *proportional to the area of the square*. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t}=-kA\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe side length of a square is given by \n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{A}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{A}}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} & =-kA \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{A}}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-kA \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-2k{A}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=2k>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-K{A}^{3/2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188290 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9609247-0e03-57ea-b5ae-e4d8317f21cd" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Contextual Problems Into Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98acc335-5a05-57d1-8371-293cd7062145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-kM+1\\,500,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375084} {:answer/id #uuid "2d341451-5f26-50af-969e-8ff3ed2e215f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-1,500M,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375085} {:answer/id #uuid "60aa858d-9503-5d2a-9bd7-87bbe3adcc86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375086} {:answer/id #uuid "3884d47f-4d7a-559f-8e29-a3f62ce9ccb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-kM-1\\,500,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375087} {:answer/id #uuid "8e937f25-0f1d-5bb9-9104-b1bda4614605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM-1\\,500,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e937f25-0f1d-5bb9-9104-b1bda4614605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM-1\\,500,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375088} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a47f3ba-08fc-5768-9a1b-fcb06056cdd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "390bc00c-f6b7-55a7-918a-e927d972b878" :question/math-academy-id "q-38250" :question/problem "The amount of money $M(t)$ in a saving account increases at a rate that's proportional to the amount currently in the account. The account holder takes $1\\,500$ dollars out of the account each year for emergencies. What is the differential equation that describes the rate of change in the amount of money in the account at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in years) since they opened the account?" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change in the number of dollars in the account per year increases in proportion to $M$ and decreases by $1\\,500.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM-1\\,500,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a (positive) constant of proportionality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba211dba-23ad-5755-b1e3-082e13be59a2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Three-Dimensional Related Rates Using Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5226f08-e0a1-5ee5-8ee1-3a2ecde686ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} = k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187549} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1d44d5-2436-5039-9972-b88953135ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} =-4πkr^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187550} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5536ab-5e17-52de-ba87-640002d4e9a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} =-kr + 2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187551} {:answer/id #uuid "1378a3ee-0e4e-5bc3-af85-43175d71add4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} =-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187552} {:answer/id #uuid "718494e0-cc4a-5d52-8f97-536ee23fb6f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dr}{dt} =-3kr" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187553}] :answer-field/id #uuid "73b83985-1ed6-5dc2-90bb-7281bf26a7e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187548}] :question/id #uuid "216b8c3f-43b1-55fb-bffc-27ac09c14aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-38252" :question/problem "Tom's spherical basketball has a hole in it. Its volume decreases at a rate that's proportional to its surface area. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t)$, of the ball. Assume that $k > 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188290 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9609247-0e03-57ea-b5ae-e4d8317f21cd" :knowledge-point/title "Translating Contextual Problems Into Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbd963ef-4415-5f3f-9ef4-510597fb2c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dA}{dt} =-kA + 2, k > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187555} {:answer/id #uuid "4698f37b-6223-585d-a89e-02849a5f453b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dA}{dt} = \\sqrt{kA} - 2, k > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187556} {:answer/id #uuid "57910d26-20d5-5742-940f-a3c57c3228d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dA}{dt} = kA + 2, k > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187557} {:answer/id #uuid "6f52c2be-20a6-53f4-8de6-0f252ae8f5c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dA}{dt} = kA - 2, k > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187558} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2b8e6e-4dd4-5293-90a2-e7f728426606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dA}{dt} = kA, k > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187559}] :answer-field/id #uuid "73794a84-57c2-5719-a752-faea2f49769e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187554} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca0e9268-1caf-523c-b9f2-33b5e344e302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-kA+2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402630} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b05b1a-5684-5d7b-b75e-a7617a17e248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{kA}-2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402631} {:answer/id #uuid "86f4b722-93dd-52c5-a40c-7b44b017ce4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA-2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402632} {:answer/id #uuid "5356c73e-9cfd-516a-8bfe-6eeb1eccf437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA+2,\\,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402633} {:answer/id #uuid "f351aa2b-4c9b-5a80-930e-82035730d517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA,\\,\\,k>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86f4b722-93dd-52c5-a40c-7b4